            <ArticleTitle>68Ga-PSMA PET/CT Imaging and 153Sm-EDTMP Bone Pain Palliation Therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e353-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000001230</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ga-labeled prostate-specific membrane antigen (PSMA) is a potential tool in the imaging of recurrent prostate cancer. Ga-PSMA imaging is also useful for radiotherapy planning and in targeted therapy with Lu-PSMA. A few case reports regarding the use of Ga-PSMA in nonprostate cancer malignancies are also reported. We describe the use of Ga-PSMA imaging before Sm-EDTMP bone pain palliation therapy in a 58-year-old hormone refractory prostate cancer patient with extensive bone metastases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
